#: ../../language/error_codes/E4236.md:1
msgid "E4236"
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/error_codes/E4236.md:3
msgid "Compiler diagnostic name: `lexscan_target_ambiguous`."
msgstr "コンパイラ診断名：`lexscan_target_ambiguous`。"

#: ../../language/error_codes/E4236.md:5
msgid ""
"The target of `lexscan` supports both `@lexbuf.Scannable` and "
"`@lexbuf.BytesScannable`, so the compiler cannot choose text or byte "
"scanning. The regex cases do not resolve this ambiguity."
msgstr "`lexscan` の対象が `@lexbuf.Scannable` と `@lexbuf.BytesScannable` の両方をサポートするため、コンパイラはテキストとバイトのどちらをスキャンするか選べません。正規表現の分岐ではこの曖昧さは解消できません。"

#: ../../language/error_codes/E4236.md:9
msgid "Erroneous example"
msgstr "誤った例"

#: ../../language/error_codes/E4236.md:11
msgid ""
"///|\n"
"pub fn[T : @lexbuf.Scannable + @lexbuf.BytesScannable] scan_word(\n"
"  target : T,\n"
") -> Bool {\n"
"  lexscan target {\n"
"    re\"^[a-z]+\" => true\n"
"    _ => false\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/error_codes/E4236.md:15
msgid "Suggestion"
msgstr "修正案"

#: ../../language/error_codes/E4236.md:17
msgid ""
"For a generic function, require only the scanning trait it needs. For a "
"concrete type that implements both traits, use a wrapper that implements "
"just one."
msgstr "ジェネリック関数では、必要なスキャン用トレイトだけを要求してください。両トレイトを実装する具体的な型には、片方だけを実装するラッパーを使ってください。"

#: ../../language/error_codes/E4236.md:20
msgid ""
"///|\n"
"pub fn[T : @lexbuf.Scannable] scan_word(target : T) -> Bool {\n"
"  lexscan target {\n"
"    re\"^[a-z]+\" => true\n"
"    _ => false\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
